# Docker build context rules for every image built from the repo root
# (infra/docker/docker-compose.build.yml, apps/<app>/Dockerfile). Owned by window 5 per
# docs/ownership.md; granted by REQUEST #70.
#
# The first rule is the one that matters. The Dockerfiles do `COPY apps ./apps`, so without it an
# apps/<app>/.env would be baked into an image layer, where it survives every later `RUN rm` and
# ships to the registry. There is no such file today; the point is that there never can be.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Installed inside the image from the lockfile — this is why the Dockerfiles no longer need
# `RUN find apps packages -maxdepth 3 -type d -name node_modules -prune -exec rm -rf {} +`.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs belong to the build stage. Copying a developer's stale one into the context is waste,
# and would be actively misleading if a build step were ever skipped.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.medusa
**/.turbo

# Terraform provider binaries: ~710 MB per environment (see REQUEST #55).
**/.terraform

# Nothing in the image needs history, logs or coverage.
.git
.gitattributes
**/*.log
**/coverage
